    {
      "id": "claim_a463f92843564fe5b2da9b2d2a90cf19",
      "statement": "The onMetaData key-decryption SUCCESS path re-reads receivingFiles[id] and null-guards it before assigning aesKey (PR #101): the entry is deniable/removable during the decryption await (post-#76 the list UI shows Accept/Deny on WaitingAccept entries; onDeny deletes the entry), and an unguarded post-await receivingFiles[id].aesKey assignment would throw 'Cannot set properties of undefined (setting aesKey)' as an unhandled rejection outside any try/catch (the data-channel onmessage caller does not await onMetaData) when a Deny landed in that window — no toast, no error state, and no EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR/EVENT_RECEIVER_REJECT for the sender. The guarded handler returns quietly for a removed entry. Pinned by tests/receiver-metadata-key-null-guard.test.mjs, which mirrors the pre- and post-fix shapes with a mocked decrypt that runs onRemove before it settles plus a static guard on the real component. The sibling key-unwrap CATCH path's receivingFiles[id].error write is null-guarded separately in PR #103 (see that claim), so both post-await writes are now guarded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/receiver/Receiver.svelte#L91-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42b8bed04d6733747b8fc5b637fbe86d221a61b33c2a099529deaf9e81e48c83:"
        },
        {
