        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_748d37edbe934b2886df5cf8d63b6c4e",
      "statement": "The onMetaData key-decryption CATCH path (PR #103) re-reads receivingFiles[id] and null-guards it before the error write: when the entry was denied/removed during the decryption await, the catch returns quietly instead of throwing an unhandled TypeError on the receivingFiles[id].error assignment — the second unguarded post-await write in onMetaData, fixed after the success path's aesKey write (PR #101). Without this guard, a Deny landing in the decryption window would leave receivingFiles[id] undefined, so the catch's error-assignment would throw 'Cannot set properties of undefined (setting error)' as an unhandled rejection outside any try/catch, and the addToastMessage + send(EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR) that follow would never run, leaving the sender's file stuck in WaitingAccept forever. tests/receiver-metadata-key-catch-null-guard.test.mjs (PR #103) pins it with a mocked decrypt that denies the entry mid-await plus a static guard on the real component.",
      "evidence": [
